# current_region_stack.tkr — the §16 arena crumb D fixture. `main.tks` runs the current-region-stack
# gate over the raw mmap `fundo`: with nothing entered the current region is the root; entering a
# child makes it current so an `alloc` lands in the child while the root's chunk list is untouched;
# leaving restores the root so the next `alloc` lands in the root and at a distinct address; and
# dropping the child removes it from the live-region registry while the root and its sentinel word
# survive. Every check asserts an observable — a region identity, a chunk membership, a registry
# membership, a surviving word — never the mere absence of a crash. All-pass reports exit code 42;
# any other code names the invariant that broke.

Feature: current_region_stack — the §16 Teko arena current-region stack (crumb D), exit 42 on all-pass

  Scenario: current_region_discipline_holds — enter/alloc-to-child/leave/alloc-to-root/drop-child all hold
    When the program is built and run
    Then it exits 42
